From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump qs 6.16.1->6.17.0 and follow-redirects 1.16.1->1.16.2

Upstream: https://github.com/ljharb/qs/commit/234d5051f5071efaa025a7ca9e4d34a56a460a1b
Upstream: https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/commit/b0a7751e9cd64cd8eeb6ec67d2f206a9cc88d3f8

Bump vendored qs 6.16.1 -> 6.17.0 (CVE-2026-110910): qs.stringify with
allowEmptyArrays: true skips encoding the key of an empty array, so a
key containing & or = becomes query string syntax and allows parameter
injection. Fixed in 6.17.0 by encoding the key through the same encoder
path used for all other keys.

Bump vendored follow-redirects 1.16.1 -> 1.16.2 (CVE-2026-116689): the
sensitiveHeaders option is checked with instanceof Array, which returns
false for arrays created in a different JS realm; the header list is
then silently replaced with an empty array, allowing credential headers
to be forwarded to cross-origin redirect targets. Fixed in 1.16.2 by
using Array.isArray instead.

Regenerated yarn.lock; yarn cache entries updated in Source3.

